The RISC-V interpreter fixes and PWM backend derive from our CHGame ATM
Soundtracks port. Mystic Balloon retains ATM's pulse/square/saw waveforms,
enables its original sound-effect overlay, and uses the song's tempo divider.
No NES/Game Boy arrangements from the soundtrack demo are included.

Per-game SD save storage (1.4.0): the private FAT reader and SPI driver in
MysticBalloon/src/savecard/ are adapted from CHGame/CHSd by bateske, MIT licensed.
See MysticBalloon/SAVE-CARD-LICENSE and MysticBalloon/src/savecard/upstream.json. The adaptation adds
single-sector writes to a preallocated save file and leaves FAT metadata
unchanged during gameplay.
